{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-36288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=-1$ and the plane $y=2$ onto the $xz$-plane?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $y=2$, we substitute $y=2$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+1-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8} & =-2 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the hyperbola: $-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94af275adea2e182f1a31f4a527688f6019066ce9da351ff0f1ea11bb2cb041c"} {"question" "q-36288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbola: $-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=1$"] ["text" "A hyperbola: $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=1$"] ["text" "A hyperbola: $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=-1$"] ["text" "An ellipse: $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=1$"] ["text" "Two parallel lines: $z=2x\\pm 4$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperbola: $-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=1$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet  $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1 & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =3(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1) \\\\ (z+1) & =\\pm \\sqrt{3(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1$, including its boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\ge 1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94af275adea2e182f1a31f4a527688f6019066ce9da351ff0f1ea11bb2cb041c"} {"question" "q-36388" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36388" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}<1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\ge 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}<0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\ge 0}"] ["text" "The entire $xy$-plane"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36388" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\ge 1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2} & =9((x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the ellipse $(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1,$ which includes the boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\ge 1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36465" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94af275adea2e182f1a31f4a527688f6019066ce9da351ff0f1ea11bb2cb041c"} {"question" "q-36465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\ge 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\le 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}<1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\ge 1}"] ["text" "The entire $xy$-plane"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-36465" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}\\ge 1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-71859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet  $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{5}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-71859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{5} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}-1 & =\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{5} \\\\ (z-1)^{2} & =5(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}-1) \\\\ (z-1) & =\\pm \\sqrt{5(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}-1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8} & \\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the exterior of the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}=1$, including its boundary.\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}\\ge 1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-71859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94af275adea2e182f1a31f4a527688f6019066ce9da351ff0f1ea11bb2cb041c"} {"question" "q-71859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-71859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}<1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}\\ge 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}\\le 1}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}<0}"] ["math" "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}>0}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-71859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{8}\\ge 1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-71957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-71957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{6}=1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola in $xy$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-71957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "94af275adea2e182f1a31f4a527688f6019066ce9da351ff0f1ea11bb2cb041c"} {"question" "q-71957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-71957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}=1"] ["math" "2{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}=4"] ["math" "2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=-2"] ["math" "2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=4"] ["math" "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"} {"question" "q-71957" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059129/state.json" "file_sha256" "294641a5f3e32de277aa0630f5e19512e55c32ef5904e446c3053362535e07db"}] "usage" {"q-36465" []} "basis" 1921 "retractions" [[17592186124904 :question/problem "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $(x - 2)^{2} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} - \\frac{z^{2}}{9} = 1$, find the domain of $z = z(x, y)$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186122447 17592186122448 17592186122449 17592186122450 17592186122451] "immutable_fields" [[17592186122446 :answer-field/correct] [17592186122446 :answer-field/id] [17592186122446 :answer-field/key] [17592186122446 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
